      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Priority list\n1. **`#hero`** (founder bio section, img + p) — ties for the largest rendered block on the page (65,728px²) and is the first thing a viewer reads; getting its broken-image icon, alt text, and bio copy exactly right matters most.\n2. **`#specs`** (spec row, img + p) — equally large (65,728px²) and directly below `#hero`. It shares `#hero`'s markup shape (img+p wrapped in a div/section), which red-twine flagged at 0.65 confidence, but the content is an unrelated product spec, not a bio — per the page's own title (\"Coincidental shape\") and the instructions, I'm treating this as coincidental repetition, not a shared component, and building each section as its own distinct markup block.\n\nFindings: the raw HTML has no `<style>`/`<link>` tags at all, and windtailor confirms zero custom color/spacing/font tokens on `body` — just the UA-default 8px margin. Both images (`/founder.jpg`, `/spec-icon.svg`) are root-relative paths that don't resolve even in the original (rendered as broken-image icons with alt text), confirmed by the original screenshot. This is a plain, unstyled page — I'll preserve that rather than inventing styling, and keep the same broken hotlink paths rather than fabricating working image URLs."
    },
    {
      "type": "tool_use",
