    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The final clone is written to the required path. Summary:\n\n**What the page actually is:** A minimal two-section page (\"Coincidental shape\") with zero custom CSS — raw curl confirmed no `<style>`/`<link>` tags at all, and windtailor's measurement of `body` found only the UA-default 8px margin, no custom colors, spacing, or fonts. This wasn't a styling job, it was a faithful-reproduction job.\n\n**Componentization decision:** red-twine matched `#hero` and `#specs` as a repeated shape (`section(div(img,p))`, confidence 0.65). I deliberately did *not* merge them into one shared component — reading the actual content showed one is a founder-bio narrative and the other is a product spec row, unrelated in purpose despite identical markup shape. The page's own title (\"Coincidental shape\") corroborates that this convergence is intentional-in-the-fixture but not semantically meaningful, so each section was built as its own distinct block per the task's guidance on shape-only matches.\n\n**Special handling:** Both `<img>` sources (`/founder.jpg`, `/spec-icon.svg`) are root-relative paths that don't resolve even in the original — confirmed via the original screenshot, which shows broken-image icons with alt text rendered. Per the out-of-scope-hosting instruction, I preserved these exact hotlink paths rather than fixing or replacing them, since faithfully reproducing includes reproducing the broken state.\n\n**Tailwind approach:** Loaded via CDN as required, but with `corePlugins.preflight: false`. Tailwind's default preflight reset (zero margins, 1.5 line-height, sans-serif base font) would have actively fought this page's fidelity rather than helped it, since every pixel of the real layout comes from the browser's own UA stylesheet with no overrides. Disabling preflight let the markup render with true browser defaults, matching the source exactly.\n\n**Screenshot comparison (2 rounds):**\n- Round 1 (Tailwind preflight active, with `m-2`/`block` classes patched back in): 0.76% pixel diff — a slight vertical drift from Tailwind's line-height reset accumulating across the two stacked sections.\n- Round 2 (preflight disabled, plain semantic markup): odiff reported 0 changed pixels, exit code 0 — a pixel-perfect match (clone screenshot is byte-identical in size to the original).\n\nAll screenshots (`original.png`, `clone-round1.png`, `diff-round1.png`, `clone-round2.png`) are saved in the run directory alongside `clone.html`."
    }
